# React Patterns

## File structure

```
src/
  components/ui/       # Reusable primitives (Button, Input, Card, Select)
  components/layout/   # AppShell, role-specific layouts
  components/auth/     # ProtectedRoute, guards
  contexts/            # AuthContext
  lib/                 # supabase client, types, helpers
  pages/{auth,superadmin,company}/
```

## Components

- Functional components only; typed props interfaces
- Pages are thin — data fetching + layout composition, not heavy logic
- New authenticated pages: wrap in existing layout via `App.tsx` routes
- New nav items: add to layout's `navItems` array, not ad-hoc links

## Supabase in components

```tsx
// ✅ Query with typed results
const { data, error } = await supabase.from('companies').select('*')
if (error) setError(error.message)

// ✅ Admin user creation
await createUser({ email, password, full_name, role, company_id })
```

- Never import or expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in frontend
- Respect RLS — queries must work under the logged-in user's permissions

## Forms

- Use `Input`, `Select`, `Button` from `components/ui`
- Grid layout: `grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2`
- Show errors inline below the form in `text-sm text-red-600`
